B.TN=new A.cd(1,B.aj,B.aE,"Rishabhdev","Adinath, Vrishabhnath","Bull","A bull (vrishabh) \u2014 strong, patient and hard-working.","King Nabhiraj","Queen Marudevi","Ayodhya","Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","500 dhanush","84 lakh purva","Purimtal (Prayag), under a banyan tree","Kailash (Ashtapad)","Long, long ago people did not know how to farm, write or make things. King Rishabhdev lovingly taught them farming, writing, counting and many crafts. One day, while watching the dancer Nilanjana, she suddenly passed away in front of him. He understood that nothing in this world lasts forever. He gave his kingdom to his sons Bharat and Bahubali, became a Digambar muni and meditated for a very long time. After a long fast, King Shreyans offered him sugarcane juice \u2014 that day is celebrated as Akshaya Tritiya. He attained Keval Gyan and became the first Tirthankar, showing everyone the path of dharma.",'His eldest son Bharat became the first Chakravarti (emperor), and our country is called "Bharat" after him.')
B.TP=new A.cd(2,B.aj,B.aE,"Ajitnath","","Elephant","An elephant (gaj) \u2014 strong yet gentle and wise.","King Jitshatru","Queen Vijaysena","Ayodhya","Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","450 dhanush","72 lakh purva","Ayodhya","Sammed Shikharji",'Ajitnath was born in Ayodhya, in the same family as Rishabhdev. He ruled as a kind and fair king. One night he saw a meteor (shooting star) shine brightly and then vanish, and he thought, "Everything in this world is like that \u2014 here for a moment, then gone." He left his kingdom, became a Digambar muni and by deep meditation won over anger, pride, greed and attachment. He attained Keval Gyan and became the second Tirthankar.','"Ajit" means "one who can never be defeated". Sagar, the second Chakravarti (emperor), lived in his time.')
B.Jy={today:0}
B.b8=new A.dn(B.Jy,1,t.fF)
B.TU=new A.cd(3,B.aj,B.b8,"Sambhavnath","","Horse","A horse (ashva) \u2014 fast, energetic and loyal.","King Dridharajya (also called Jitari)","Queen Sushena","Shravasti","Shravasti district, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","400 dhanush","60 lakh purva","Shravasti","Sammed Shikharji","Sambhavnath was born a prince in Shravasti. Even while ruling as a king, his heart was always calm and kind. Watching the clouds in the sky form and then melt away, he understood that the pleasures of the world also do not stay. He became a Digambar muni, did deep tapasya, attained Keval Gyan and became the third Tirthankar, teaching everyone to live with ahimsa and truth.","Shravasti, his birthplace, is in today's Uttar Pradesh and is a Jain tirth kshetra.")
B.TL=new A.cd(4,B.aj,B.aE,"Abhinandannath","","Monkey","A monkey (kapi) \u2014 reminds us to calm our jumpy, restless mind.","King Swayamvar (also called Samvar)","Queen Siddhartha","Ayodhya","Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","350 dhanush","50 lakh purva","Ayodhya","Sammed Shikharji","Abhinandannath was born in Ayodhya and brought great joy to everyone. He ruled wisely. One day he saw the clouds in the sky form the shape of a beautiful city (a gandharva nagar) \u2014 and a moment later it melted away. He understood that the pleasures of the world vanish just like that, and that real happiness is inside the soul. He gave up his kingdom, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the fourth Tirthankar.",'"Abhinandan" means "one who brings joy and is praised by all".')
B.U0=new A.cd(5,B.aj,B.aE,"Sumatinath","","Chakva (ruddy goose)","A chakva \u2014 a reddish-orange water bird, also called the ruddy goose.","King Megharath","Queen Mangala","Ayodhya","Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","300 dhanush","40 lakh purva","Ayodhya","Sammed Shikharji","Sumatinath was born in Ayodhya. Even as a child he always chose the right and wise thing to do. As king he looked after his people like a father. One day he remembered his past lives (jati-smaran) and saw how his soul had wandered through birth after birth. Wanting to be free, he became a Digambar muni, meditated deeply, attained Keval Gyan and became the fifth Tirthankar.",'"Sumati" means "good wisdom" \u2014 someone with a pure, wise mind.')
B.AE=new A.G(1,0.7529411764705882,0.2235294117647059,0.16862745098039217,B.h)
B.ku=new A.m0("Red","\u0932\u093e\u0932",B.AE,1,"red")
B.U1=new A.cd(6,B.ku,B.aE,"Padmaprabhu","Padmaprabha","Lotus","A lotus (padma / kamal) \u2014 it grows in mud yet stays clean, like a pure soul.","King Dharan","Queen Susima","Kaushambi","Kaushambi (Kosam), near Prayagraj, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","250 dhanush","30 lakh purva","Kaushambi","Sammed Shikharji","Padmaprabhu was born in Kaushambi. His body shone with a reddish glow, like a red lotus. While he was ruling as king, he remembered his past lives (jati-smaran), and his attachment to the world fell away. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the sixth Tirthankar.","Padampura (near Jaipur, Rajasthan) is a famous Digambar atishay kshetra of Bhagwan Padmaprabhu.")
B.Ao=new A.G(1,0.1803921568627451,0.5450980392156862,0.3411764705882353,B.h)
B.kv=new A.m0("Green","\u0939\u0930\u093e",B.Ao,3,"green")
B.U2=new A.cd(7,B.kv,B.b8,"Suparshvanath","","Swastika","The swastika \u2014 its four arms remind us of the four gatis (states of life): heavenly beings, humans, animals and hell beings.","King Supratishtha","Queen Prithvisena","Varanasi (Kashi)","Varanasi (Bhadaini area), Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","200 dhanush","20 lakh purva","Varanasi (Kashi)","Sammed Shikharji","Suparshvanath was born in Varanasi. He was gentle and loved all living beings. Seeing how the seasons change and green leaves turn dry and fall, he understood that the body too changes and does not last. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the seventh Tirthankar.","Varanasi is the birthplace of two Tirthankars \u2014 Suparshvanath and Parshvanath.")
B.AI=new A.G(1,0.9686274509803922,0.9686274509803922,0.9490196078431372,B.h)
B.kt=new A.m0("White","\u0938\u092b\u093c\u0947\u0926 (\u0927\u0935\u0932)",B.AI,2,"white")
B.TK=new A.cd(8,B.kt,B.b8,"Chandraprabhu","Chandraprabha","Crescent moon","A crescent moon (ardha-chandra) \u2014 cool, calm and bright.","King Mahasen","Queen Lakshmana","Chandrapuri","Chandravati village, near Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","150 dhanush","10 lakh purva","Chandrapuri","Sammed Shikharji","Chandraprabhu was born in Chandrapuri. His body was white and shining, like the moon, and his nature was cool and peaceful. One day, while ruling as king, he saw a flash of lightning light up the sky and vanish in a moment. He understood that life, too, passes just as quickly. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the eighth Tirthankar.","Tijara (Rajasthan) is a famous Digambar atishay kshetra of Bhagwan Chandraprabhu.")
B.TI=new A.cd(9,B.kt,B.b8,"Pushpadant","Suvidhinath","Makar (crocodile)","A makar \u2014 a crocodile, a strong creature of the water.","King Sugriv","Queen Jayrama","Kakandi","Khukhundoo, Deoria district, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","100 dhanush","2 lakh purva","Kakandi","Sammed Shikharji","Pushpadant was born in Kakandi. He was so pure and kind that his goodness spread like the fragrance of flowers. After ruling for a long time, one night he saw a meteor (shooting star) blaze across the sky and disappear. Knowing that nothing in the world lasts, he left the palace, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the ninth Tirthankar.",'He is also called Suvidhinath \u2014 "one who shows the right way of doing things".')
B.U4=new A.cd(10,B.aj,B.b8,"Shitalnath","","Kalpavriksha","The Kalpavriksha \u2014 a wish-fulfilling tree from the scriptures that gives whatever is needed.","King Dridharath","Queen Sunanda","Bhadrikapuri (Bhaddilpur)","Bhadrakali, near Itkhori, Chatra district, Jharkhand","Ikshvaku","90 dhanush","1 lakh purva","Bhadrikapuri","Sammed Shikharji","Shitalnath was born in Bhadrikapuri. He was calm and cool like shade on a hot day, and his words brought peace to everyone. One winter morning he saw frost covering everything \u2014 and then watched it melt away in the sun. He understood that the body and the world melt away just like that, but the soul is eternal. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the tenth Tirthankar.",'"Shital" means "cool and calming".')
B.TX=new A.cd(11,B.aj,B.b8,"Shreyansnath","","Rhinoceros","A rhinoceros (gainda) \u2014 strong and steady.","King Vishnu","Queen Sunanda (also called Vishnushri)","Simhapuri (Sarnath)","Singhpur village, Sarnath, near Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","80 dhanush","84 lakh years","Simhapuri","Sammed Shikharji","Shreyansnath was born in Simhapuri. He always did what was good for others. After ruling his kingdom well, he watched the beauty of spring fade and the leaves dry up and fall. He realised that everything in the world changes, and that the greatest good is to free the soul. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the eleventh Tirthankar.",'"Shreyans" means "the most excellent, the best". His birthplace is near today\'s Sarnath, close to Varanasi.')
B.TJ=new A.cd(12,B.ku,B.aE,"Vasupujya","Vasupujya Swami","Buffalo","A buffalo (mahish) \u2014 strong and patient.","King Vasupujya","Queen Jayavati","Champapuri","Champanagar, Bhagalpur, Bihar","Ikshvaku","70 dhanush","72 lakh years","Champapuri","Champapuri (Mandargiri)","Vasupujya was born in Champapuri. He never married and never became king \u2014 he was a bal brahmachari. While still young he chose the path of the soul, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the twelfth Tirthankar.","All five kalyanaks of Vasupujya took place at Champapuri (in today's Bihar).")
B.TZ=new A.cd(13,B.aj,B.aE,"Vimalnath","","Boar","A boar (varaha / shukar) \u2014 a wild pig with tusks.","King Kritavarma","Queen Jayshyama","Kampilya","Kampil, Farrukhabad district, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","60 dhanush","60 lakh years","Kampilya","Sammed Shikharji","Vimalnath was born in Kampilya. His mind was spotless and clear like clean water. Seeing snow and frost melt away in the sun, he understood that worldly things do not last. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the thirteenth Tirthankar.",'"Vimal" means "pure, without any stain".')
B.TO=new A.cd(14,B.aj,B.aE,"Anantnath","","Sehi (porcupine)","A sehi \u2014 a porcupine, a small animal covered in long quills.","King Simhasena","Queen Jayshyama (also called Sarvashyama)","Ayodhya","Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Ikshvaku","50 dhanush","30 lakh years","Ayodhya","Sammed Shikharji","Anantnath was born in Ayodhya. He ruled with kindness and justice. One night he saw a meteor (shooting star) fall and vanish. Knowing that the world does not last, but the soul has endless (anant) knowledge and joy hidden inside it, he left the palace to uncover it. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the fourteenth Tirthankar.",'"Anant" means "endless" \u2014 like the endless knowledge and joy of a pure soul.')
B.TQ=new A.cd(15,B.aj,B.b8,"Dharmanath","","Vajra","A vajra \u2014 a thunderbolt-shaped weapon, a sign of unbreakable strength.","King Bhanu","Queen Suprabha (also called Suvrata)","Ratnapuri","Ronahi (Ratnapuri), near Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh","Kuru","45 dhanush","10 lakh years","Ratnapuri","Sammed Shikharji","Dharmanath was born in Ratnapuri. From childhood he loved dharma \u2014 truth, kindness and self-control. While ruling as king, one night he saw a meteor (shooting star) streak across the sky and vanish, and he decided not to waste his precious human life. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the fifteenth Tirthankar, teaching everyone what true dharma is.",'"Dharma" means the true nature of things and the right way to live.')
B.U_=new A.cd(16,B.aj,B.aE,"Shantinath","","Deer","A deer (mrig) \u2014 gentle, peaceful and harmless.","King Vishvasen","Queen Aira","Hastinapur",u.I,"Ikshvaku","40 dhanush","1 lakh years","Hastinapur","Sammed Shikharji","In an earlier life, as King Megharath, he protected a frightened pigeon that was being chased by a hawk \u2014 he was even ready to give his own body to save it. Born in Hastinapur as Shantinath, he became a Chakravarti, the emperor of all six parts of Bharat. Yet he gave up that huge empire, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the sixteenth Tirthankar, spreading peace everywhere.","Shantinath was a Tirthankar, a Chakravarti (emperor) and a Kamdev (most beautiful person) \u2014 all three in one life!")
B.U3=new A.cd(17,B.aj,B.aE,"Kunthunath","","Goat","A goat (aj) \u2014 simple and humble.","King Surasen","Queen Shrikanta","Hastinapur",u.I,"Kuru","35 dhanush","95,000 years","Hastinapur","Sammed Shikharji","Kunthunath was born in Hastinapur. He was very kind even to the tiniest creatures (kunthu means a tiny insect). He became a Chakravarti emperor. One day he remembered his past lives (jati-smaran) and saw that ruling the world had never made his soul truly happy. He gave it all up, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the seventeenth Tirthankar.","Like Shantinath, he too was a Tirthankar, a Chakravarti and a Kamdev.")
B.TV=new A.cd(18,B.aj,B.aE,"Aranath","Arahnath","Fish","A fish (matsya) \u2014 always moving, yet at home in the water.","King Sudarshan","Queen Mitrasena","Hastinapur",u.I,"Kuru","30 dhanush","84,000 years","Hastinapur","Sammed Shikharji","Aranath was born in Hastinapur. He too became a Chakravarti emperor. One day he watched a beautiful cloud in the autumn sky suddenly break up and vanish. He understood that even the greatest empire does not last. He gave it up, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the eighteenth Tirthankar.","Shantinath, Kunthunath and Aranath were all born in Hastinapur, and each was a Tirthankar, a Chakravarti and a Kamdev.")
B.TS=new A.cd(19,B.aj,B.b8,"Mallinath","","Kalash","A kalash \u2014 a sacred pot, a sign of auspiciousness and completeness.","King Kumbh","Queen Prajavati","Mithila",u.b,"Ikshvaku","25 dhanush","55,000 years","Mithila","Sammed Shikharji","Mallinath was born a prince in Mithila. He never married \u2014 he was a bal brahmachari. While still young he remembered his past lives (jati-smaran) and understood that worldly pleasures never give lasting happiness. He became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the nineteenth Tirthankar.","He is one of the five bal brahmachari Tirthankars: Vasupujya, Mallinath, Neminath, Parshvanath and Mahavir.")
B.Ay=new A.G(1,0.1411764705882353,0.23137254901960785,0.5411764705882353,B.h)
B.ks=new A.m0("Dark blue (shyam)","\u0936\u094d\u092f\u093e\u092e (\u0917\u0939\u0930\u093e \u0928\u0940\u0932\u093e)",B.Ay,4,"darkBlue")
B.TT=new A.cd(20,B.ks,B.aE,"Munisuvratnath","Munisuvrat","Tortoise","A tortoise (kachhua) \u2014 it pulls in its limbs, like we should control our senses.","King Sumitra","Queen Soma (also called Padmavati)","Rajgriha (Rajgir)","Rajgir, Nalanda district, Bihar","Harivansh","20 dhanush","30,000 years","Rajgriha","Sammed Shikharji",'Munisuvratnath was born in Rajgriha. After he had ruled for many years, something wonderful happened: his royal elephant remembered its past life and took vows of self-control, like a good shravak. The king thought, "If even an elephant can turn to dharma, why am I still tied to this world?" He became a Digambar muni, kept his vows (vrat) perfectly \u2014 as his name says \u2014 attained Keval Gyan and became the twentieth Tirthankar.',"According to Jain scriptures, Shri Ram, Lakshman and Sita lived in the time (tirth) of Munisuvratnath.")
B.TW=new A.cd(21,B.aj,B.b8,"Naminath","Nami","Blue lotus","A blue lotus (nilotpal) \u2014 a beautiful blue water flower.","King Vijay","Queen Mahadevi (also called Vapra)","Mithila",u.b,"Ikshvaku","15 dhanush","10,000 years","Mithila","Sammed Shikharji",'Naminath was born in Mithila. He was humble \u2014 "nami" means one who bows. As king he ruled with fairness. Remembering his past lives, he felt detached from the world, became a Digambar muni, attained Keval Gyan and became the twenty-first Tirthankar.',"Mithila is the birthplace of two Tirthankars \u2014 Mallinath and Naminath.")
B.TM=new A.cd(22,B.ks,B.aE,"Neminath","Arishtanemi","Conch","A conch shell (shankh) \u2014 its sound is a call to wake up.","King Samudravijay","Queen Shivadevi","Shauripur (Mahapuran: Dwarka)","Bateshwar, near Agra, Uttar Pradesh","Harivansh (Yadav)","10 dhanush","1,000 years","Girnar (Urjayant)","Girnar (Urjayant)","Neminath was a prince and a cousin of Shri Krishna. On the day of his wedding to princess Rajul, he heard many animals crying \u2014 they were locked up to be killed for the wedding feast. Full of compassion, he set all the animals free, turned his chariot around and went to Girnar mountain to become a Digambar muni. Rajul also chose the path of dharma and became an aryika. Neminath attained Keval Gyan and became the twenty-second Tirthankar.","Girnar hill in Gujarat is where he attained Keval Gyan and moksha. He was also a bal brahmachari.")
B.Jz={today:0,kevalGyan:1}
B.MH=new A.dn(B.Jz,2,t.fF)
B.TR=new A.cd(23,B.kv,B.MH,"Parshvanath","Parasnath","Snake","A snake (sarp) with a raised hood \u2014 reminding us of how Dharanendra protected him.","King Ashvasen (Mahapuran: Vishvasen)","Queen Vama (Mahapuran: Brahmi)","Varanasi (Kashi)","Bhelupur, Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh","Ugra","9 hath","100 years","Ahichchhatra","Sammed Shikharji","Prince Parshvakumar once saw a tapasvi burning a big log for his fire. With his special knowledge he knew a pair of snakes was trapped inside. He had the log split open; the dying snakes heard the Namokar Mantra and were reborn as Dharanendra and Padmavati. Parshvakumar never married. He became a Digambar muni, and while he meditated, Kamath \u2014 an enemy from past lives \u2014 attacked him with storms and heavy rain. Dharanendra came and spread his great hood over him like an umbrella. Parshvanath stayed perfectly calm, attained Keval Gyan and became the twenty-third Tirthankar.","Parasnath hill \u2014 Sammed Shikharji in Jharkhand \u2014 is named after him.")
B.TY=new A.cd(24,B.aj,B.b8,"Mahavir Swami","Vardhaman, Vir, Ativir, Sanmati","Lion","A lion (simha) \u2014 brave and fearless.","King Siddharth","Queen Trishala (Priyakarini)","Kundalpur (Kundagram)","Kundalpur near Nalanda, Bihar (many now say Vaishali, Bihar)","Nath (Gyatri)","7 hath","72 years","Bank of the Rijukula river, near Jrimbhikagram","Pavapuri",'As a child he was called Vardhaman. Once a deva, wanting to test his courage, took the form of a huge snake while the children were playing near a tree. The other children ran away, but Vardhaman fearlessly calmed the snake \u2014 so he was called "Mahavir", the great brave one. He never married. At the age of 30 he left the palace and became a Digambar muni. After 12 years of silent meditation and tapasya, he attained Keval Gyan and became the twenty-fourth Tirthankar. He taught ahimsa (non-violence), truth and aparigraha (not being greedy).',"We celebrate Mahavir Jayanti on Chaitra Shukla 13, and Diwali is the day he attained moksha at Pavapuri.")
